    board(toolchain): close RELEASE-OB-019 — Go floor 1.26.11, CI pins, judge PASS
    
    Work landed at 17258b9e (origin/master): go.mod moves `go 1.26.9` -> `go 1.26.11`,
    all four ci.yml setup-go inputs pin the exact patch, README prerequisites and the
    bootstrap tarball move to 1.26.11, and the GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.11 release prefix is
    documented in README, Makefile and CHANGELOG. go.sum is untouched; no source or
    dependency edit is involved.
    
    Why 1.26.11 and not the row's original 1.26.10: 1.26.10 closes GO-2026-6809
    (crypto/x509) but GO-2026-6859 (net/http) needs 1.26.11, so "govulncheck reports
    zero" is only reachable at 1.26.11. The row's acceptance criteria were re-scoped
    accordingly before close rather than shipping a floor that still trips the scanner.
    
    Evidence on the pushed tip: govulncheck ./... -> "No vulnerabilities found." (2
    findings at 1.26.9), bare build links go1.26.11 (go version -m), make test rc0,
    go vet clean, 4/4 setup-go pins read 1.26.11. Tier-2 judge verdict 2aadd1ed = PASS,
    written against merge commit d9783275 whose five changed blobs are byte-identical to
    17258b9e (verified per-file), so the verdict binds to the pushed tree by content.
    CI run 43944086284 on 17258b9e: success, all six jobs (incl. "Go 1.26.11").
    
    The judge flagged two uncovered failure paths at close — a future CI edit
    reintroducing a floating '1.26' pin, and the README tarball drifting behind go.mod.
    The follow-up row for a drift guard was drafted but its creation was refused by the
    approval gate, so it is not on the board yet; it needs the owner's consent.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
