ervice code. Spec: docs/observability-spec.md section 5 and section 7. ACCEPTANCE: (1) In Prometheus, `up{job=\"off-by-one\"}` returns exactly 1 series with value 1 and labels product=\"off-by-one\". (2) `count(count by (__name__) ({__name__=~\"obo_.+\", product=\"off-by-one\"}))` >= 12 - i.e. at least 12 obo_* metric families are actually stored server-side, not merely exposed. (3) After a seed run, `obo_seed_completion_timestamp_seconds` (or the chosen record name) advances and carries the run's exit status. (4) docs/observability-spec.md section 5 names the real job name and the real target host - no placeholders remain.","acceptance_criteria":"Prometheus up{job=\"off-by-one\"} == 1 with product=\"off-by-one\"; count(count by (__name__) ({__name__=~\"obo_.+\", product=\"off-by-one\"})) >= 12; seed run advances a textfile/pushgateway completion record with exit status; docs/observability-spec.md section 5 contains no placeholders.","detail":{"spec":"docs/observability-spec.md","sections":["5","7"],"owner_note":"monitoring stack is out of repo scope; coordinate with fleet-monitor owner"}}
