+ {"id":"README-10","title":"P5 — README.md:562-569 gitreins install paragraph is a broken edit: the duplicated clause leaves 'An older recipe suggested' with no predicate","status":"pending","priority":"P5","complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-16T18:39:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T18:39:09Z","capability_tags":["docs","readme","polish"],"reasoning":"MEASURED at published tip b809d11e, `sed -n '560,570p' README.md` verbatim:\n  `gitreins` resolves through the pipx shim at `~/.local/bin/gitreins` — do NOT\n  prefix PATH with a repo venv. An older recipe suggested\n  `gitreins` is installed via pipx and available at `~/.local/bin/gitreins`\n  (the repo was renamed to `~/gitreins`), and where a similar stale venv does\n  exist, putting it first on PATH makes its tools shadow the repo interpreter\n  and falsely FAIL the tests lane on a clean tree.\nThe second sentence has no predicate: 'An older recipe suggested' is followed by a plain assertion that gitreins IS the pipx shim, then an ', and where ...' clause attached to nothing. A reader cannot tell what the older recipe said, what is wrong with it, or which instruction to follow; the two sentences also contradict each other (do not prefix PATH vs. the venv case).\nOnly the prose is wrong: the guard table at README.md:573-578 matches .gitreins/config.yaml (secrets guard on, go.build true, go.lint false, go.tests true, tests lane pinned by test_command), so the fix is a rewrite, not a table change.\nDoc severity is P5 (polish/wording) by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling — do not re-raise. ch:trace row=README-10 spec=README.md#gitreins-quality-harness wave=none:serial-sweep test=none:docs-only-row doc=README.md prompt=/home/kara/.hermes/skills/coding-hermes/coding-hermes-readme/SKILL.md evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/off-by-one/ev-2026-11-16/transcript-2026-11-16.txt witness=path@origin:README.md verdict=none:open-finding commit=none:open memory=none:not-written","acceptance_criteria":"README.md 'GitReins Quality Harness' prose (lines ~562-569) becomes one grammatical instruction that states: gitreins resolves through the pipx shim at ~/.local/bin/gitreins; do not put a repo venv ahead of it on PATH; the tests lane is interpreter-pinned in .gitreins/config.yaml (test_command), so PATH ordering does not change the lane's interpreter.\nProve by quoting the rewritten paragraph and `grep -c 'An older recipe suggested' README.md` (0, or a single grammatical sentence that states what the old recipe claimed and why it is wrong).\nREJECTS: editing install instructions in other files as part of this row (REVIEW-OB-001/-004 already swept the fleet recipes).","detail":{"fingerprint":"0540136c8aa3bed182db97421837af339831c58a0c654bf5e8504481d9892dc4","evidence":[{"run_id":"off-by-one-readme-2026-11-16-18-00-12","ts":"2026-11-16T18:39:09Z","tree_fp":"7cfdf7cb1d04e026285709a56edb06d80247081dd77e955d186910311c684992","artifacts":["/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/off-by-one/ev-2026-11-16/transcript-2026-11-16.txt"]}]},"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"type":null}
+ {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60-R2","title":"P4 — RECURRENCE of DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60: README 'Install from a release' still hardcodes V=v0.2.0 after v0.3.0 shipped, so the documented first-run path installs the previous release","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-16T18:39:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T18:39:09Z","capability_tags":["docs","readme","release-boundary","recurrence"],"reasoning":"MEASURED at published tip b809d11e (README.md blob 8b6ab356...). README.md:451 sets `V=v0.2.0` inside '### Install from a release (no toolchain needed)'.\nExecuted the block verbatim as written (lines 450-463, in a non-checkout dir with a fresh HOME): the four curl/sha256sum/chmod steps succeed ('off-by-one-v0.2.0-linux-amd64: OK') and the binary self-reports `off-by-one v0.2.0`.\nCurrent release boundary: `gh release list --repo totalwindupflightsystems/off-by-one` -> v0.3.0 (Latest, 2026-11-04T16:52:29Z), v0.2.1, v0.2.0; `git describe --tags` at the tip is v0.3.0-31-gba00870b; CHANGELOG.md:28 carries `## [v0.3.0] - 2026-11-04`. The v0.3.0 asset was downloaded and executed in the same non-checkout dir: `off-by-one v0.3.0`.\nReader harm, measured: the v0.2.0 binary the block installs does not serve GET /metrics/prom (the v0.3.0 headline route), so a stranger following the documented install path lands one release behind the front page's feature set.\nRECURRENCE: DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60 was filed and closed for exactly this defect at v0.1.1; the snippet was bumped to v0.2.0 instead of being made self-updating, so the same rot returned at the next cut. Cite DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60 in the fix discussion; do not file a bare sibling of it.\nDoc severity is P4 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (it is a freshness defect, not a data-destroying command). ch:trace row=DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60-R2 spec=README.md#install-from-a-release wave=none:serial-sweep test=none:docs-only-row doc=README.md prompt=/home/kara/.hermes/skills/coding-hermes/coding-hermes-readme/SKILL.md evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/off-by-one/ev-2026-11-16/release-asset-2026-11-16.txt witness=release:v0.3.0 verdict=none:open-finding commit=none:open memory=none:not-written","acceptance_criteria":"The 'Install from a release' block cannot silently install a superseded release: either it derives the latest tag (e.g. from the GitHub releases/latest redirect) or it is pinned to the current release with a check that fails when the pin is not the newest tag.\nProve by executing the block verbatim in a non-checkout directory and quoting `--version` output, which must equal the newest published tag from `gh release list --repo totalwindupflightsystems/off-by-one --limit 1`; and by a repo-side check (docs/test target) that goes red when the pinned V is older than the latest tag.\nREJECTS: bumping the literal to v0.3.0 with no check (that is the exact rot that recurred twice); changing the release pipeline or cutting a new release to make the README's pin current.","detail":{"fingerprint":"e825feb6a250e56d737507b4947bd5b7bb765cd8284ac16f6a58f0a40add55e7","evidence":[{"run_id":"off-by-one-readme-2026-11-16-18-00-12","ts":"2026-11-16T18:39:09Z","tree_fp":"377a845e6f96609090ab1424e6a21ce107f7c24f0e00149ad9feefd8425c5564","artifacts":["/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/off-by-one/ev-2026-11-16/transcript-2026-11-16.txt","/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/off-by-one/ev-2026-11-16/release-asset-2026-11-16.txt"]}]},"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"type":null}
++{"id":"DEPLOY-OB-002","title":"[P1] Deploy recipe cannot end in PASS: vendored deploy/off-by-one.service caps solves at -solve-mem-mb 6144 while the root-caused host unit runs 12288, so check-deploy leg 5 (flag contract) fails on every deploy","status":"pending","priority":"P1","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-16T19:44:29Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T19:44:29Z","capability_tags":["deploy","systemd","flag-contract"],"reasoning":"MEASURED 2026-11-16 14:43 EST (ops tick off-by-one-ops-2026-11-16-18-40-31, fire 3).\n\nThe standing owner deploy command for OBS-OB-003 ends in `cd /home/kara/off-by-one && make check-deploy`, and it CANNOT reach PASS even when the install+restart succeed, because the repo's own vendored unit is stale against a root-caused host fix:\n\n  $ git show origin/master:deploy/off-by-one.service | grep -n 'solve-mem-mb'\n  55:# -solve-mem-mb 6144 (DF-OFF-BY-ONE-30): per-solve RLIMIT_AS cap applied by the\n  62:ExecStart=... -bwrap /usr/bin/bwrap -solve-mem-mb 6144\n\n  $ grep -n 'solve-mem-mb' /etc/systemd/system/off-by-one.service\n  55:# -solve-mem-mb 12288 (was 6144): per-solve RLIMIT_AS cap applied by the\n  67:ExecStart=... -bwrap /usr/bin/bwrap -solve-mem-mb 12288\n\n  $ ./scripts/check-deploy --check-flags deploy/off-by-one.service \"$(systemctl show off-by-one -p ExecStart --value)\"\n  FAIL: running unit's ExecStart flags drifted from deploy/off-by-one.service:\n    -solve-mem-mb: expected 6144, observed 12288\n  seam_rc=1\n\nThe HOST value is the correct one and is root-caused in the host unit's own comment (lines 55-58): 6144 was the value that BROKE every solve after the pi 1.5.0 install — Node 22 needs the larger RLIMIT_AS to initialise undici's fetch path, and pi-agent surfaced the abort as \"Connection error.\" on every solve (2026-11-04). Per-solve bounding still holds twice over: RLIMIT_AS=12288 MiB and the cgroup MemoryMax=8G, which binds first. So the repo is the stale artifact, not the host.\n\nConsequence: any owner-run deploy that follows the recipe lands a correct binary and then reports check-deploy FAIL at leg 5, which reads as a failed deploy and hides the real (passing) legs. This is the reason OBS-OB-003's post-deploy expectation had to be corrected; no board row owned the defect before this one (grep of tasks.jsonl for 12288/undici/lazyllhttp/solve-mem returned only already-complete rows).\n\nThree-file sync required (all inside this repo):\n  - deploy/off-by-one.service:55,62 — 6144 -> 12288 and carry the Node 22 / undici rationale comment from the host unit, so the vendored unit is the root-caused one.\n  - scripts/check-deploy-test.sh:278,594 — the two drift arms assert the failure text \"solve-mem-mb: expected 6144, observed <absent>\"; they must expect 12288 or they will fail against the corrected unit.\n  - docs/api-reference.md:807 — worked example says `--solve-mem-mb 6144`; use 12288 so the doc and the shipped unit agree.","acceptance_criteria":"PASS when all four arms are quoted with exact command + output:\n\n1) VENDORED UNIT IS ROOT-CAUSED: `git show <commit>:deploy/off-by-one.service | grep -n 'solve-mem-mb'` shows 12288 in ExecStart AND a comment recording why 6144 was reverted (Node 22 undici/lazyllhttp abort, pi 1.5.0, 2026-11-04), so the file explains itself rather than carrying a bare number.\n\n2) FLAG CONTRACT ENDS IN PASS: in a clean checkout of the commit, `./scripts/check-deploy --check-flags deploy/off-by-one.service \"$(systemctl show off-by-one -p ExecStart --value)\"` exits 0 and prints PASS, i.e. the standing owner deploy command's final leg is GREEN instead of failing on a repo-side stale value.\n\n3) HERMETIC TEST STILL BITES: `bash -n scripts/check-deploy-test.sh` exits 0 and the two drift arms (lines that assert the failure text) pass with the new expectation — the arm must still FAIL when the running unit's value differs, proven by at least one arm that feeds a deliberately different -solve-mem-mb and gets the drift message. Widening the assertion to accept either number is a REJECT.\n\n4) DOC AGREES: `git grep -n 'solve-mem-mb 6144' <commit>` returns no hits in deploy/, scripts/ or docs/ (the only permitted hit would be a historical narrative that explicitly labels 6144 as the reverted value).\n\nREJECTS: changing the host unit back to 6144 (re-breaks every solve), deleting the flag-contract leg, or relaxing it to a warning.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"9a8e50ab85efdc4e9ee6809e9aa7da304d1669163b69a2ea2735fc1a78d3b939"},"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"type":"chore"}
